; ============================================================================
;  HALLWAY  --  8.0 x 2.6 m spine of the house, 2.4 m ceiling.
;
;  Doorways: bathroom and bedroom off the -Z wall, staircase off the +Z wall.
;  The west end (-X) is the starting area; the instruction panel and the
;  physical buttons are mounted on that wall in main.tscn.
;
;  Hazards: a rug with a curled edge, and an extension cord run across the
;  walkway. Both are trip hazards rather than slip hazards, which is why the
;  cord has no SlipZone -- catching a toe on a cord is not something a
;  non-vestibular warning can honestly simulate, so it is a recognition task
;  only.
; ============================================================================

